@startuml GetWorkoutsAsync Sequence Diagram
!theme plain
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 150
skinparam BoxPadding 10

title HevyService.GetWorkoutsAsync() - Paginated Workout Retrieval with MaxResults Limit

actor "Caller" as Caller
participant "HevyService" as Service
participant "HttpClient" as HTTP
participant "Hevy API\n(v1/workouts)" as API
participant "JsonSerializer" as JSON

== Initialize Pagination Parameters ==

Caller -> Service: GetWorkoutsAsync(page=1, pageSize=10, maxResults=100)
activate Service

note right of Service
  **Method Parameters:**
  - page: Starting page (1-based)
  - pageSize: Items per page (max 10)
  - maxResults: Total items limit
end note

Service -> Service: Validate pageSize <= 10
alt #LightCoral pageSize > 10
    Service --> Caller: throw ArgumentOutOfRangeException
    note right
      Exception message:
      "pageSize cannot exceed 20 due 
      to Hevy API limitations"
    end note
else #LightGreen pageSize valid
    Service -> Service: Initialize collections
    note right of Service
      - last20Workouts = new List<HevyWorkout>()
      - currentPage = page (1)
      - totalPages = int.MaxValue
    end note
end

== Pagination Loop - Fetch All Pages Until Limit ==

loop while (currentPage <= totalPages && last20Workouts.Count < maxResults)
    
    note over Service, API
      **Iteration State:**
      - Current Page: {currentPage}
      - Workouts Collected: {last20Workouts.Count}
      - Remaining Slots: {maxResults - last20Workouts.Count}
    end note
    
    Service -> HTTP: GetAsync("/v1/workouts?page={currentPage}&pageSize={pageSize}")
    activate HTTP
    
    HTTP -> API: GET /v1/workouts?page={currentPage}&pageSize={pageSize}
    activate API
    
    note right of API
      **Request Headers:**
      - api-key: {config.ApiKey}
      - Accept: application/json
      - BaseUrl: {config.BaseUrl}
    end note
    
    API --> HTTP: HTTP Response (200 OK)
    deactivate API
    
    HTTP -> HTTP: EnsureSuccessStatusCode()
    note right of HTTP
      Validates response status.
      Throws if 4xx or 5xx error.
    end note
    
    HTTP -> HTTP: ReadAsStringAsync()
    HTTP --> Service: JSON content string
    deactivate HTTP
    
    Service -> JSON: Deserialize<HevyWorkoutsResponse>(content)
    activate JSON
    
    note right of JSON
      **Response Model:**
      {
        "workouts": [...],
        "page": int,
        "page_count": int,
        "workout_count": int
      }
    end note
    
    JSON --> Service: HevyWorkoutsResponse object
    deactivate JSON
    
    alt #LightCoral Response is null OR no workouts
        Service -> Service: break loop
        note right of Service
          No more workouts available.
          Exit pagination early.
        end note
    else #LightGreen Valid response with workouts
        
        alt #LightBlue First iteration (currentPage == page)
            Service -> Service: totalPages = workoutsResponse.PageCount
            note right of Service
              Update totalPages from API response.
              This determines loop boundary.
            end note
        end
        
        Service -> Service: Calculate remainingSlots
        note right of Service
          remainingSlots = 
            maxResults - last20Workouts.Count
          
          Ensures we don't exceed maxResults
        end note
        
        Service -> Service: workoutsToAdd = workoutsResponse.Workouts.Take(remainingSlots)
        note right of Service
          Take only enough workouts to fill
          remaining slots up to maxResults limit
        end note
        
        Service -> Service: last20Workouts.AddRange(workoutsToAdd)
        note right of Service
          Add workouts to collection.
          May add fewer than pageSize
          if near maxResults limit.
        end note
        
        Service -> Service: currentPage++
        note right of Service
          Increment page counter
          for next iteration
        end note
    end
    
    alt #LightGreen last20Workouts.Count >= maxResults
        Service -> Service: exit loop (maxResults reached)
        note right of Service
          Maximum results limit reached.
          Stop fetching additional pages.
        end note
    end
    
    alt #LightGreen currentPage > totalPages
        Service -> Service: exit loop (all pages fetched)
        note right of Service
          All available pages retrieved.
          No more data from API.
        end note
    end
    
end

== Return Results ==

Service --> Caller: List<HevyWorkout> (last20Workouts)
deactivate Service

note over Caller, Service
  **Returned Collection:**
  - Size: min(total workouts, maxResults)
  - Contains workouts from consecutive pages
  - Respects both pagination and maxResults limits
end note

== Error Scenarios ==

note over Caller, JSON
  **Potential Exceptions:**
  
  1. **ArgumentOutOfRangeException**
     - Thrown when: pageSize > 10
     - Message: "pageSize cannot exceed 20 due to Hevy API limitations"
  
  2. **HttpRequestException**
     - Network connectivity issues
     - DNS resolution failures
     - Connection timeouts
  
  3. **TaskCanceledException**
     - Request timeout exceeded
     - Cancellation token triggered
  
  4. **Exception from EnsureSuccessStatusCode()**
     - 401 Unauthorized: Invalid/missing API key
     - 403 Forbidden: Access denied
     - 404 Not Found: Invalid endpoint
     - 429 Too Many Requests: Rate limit exceeded
     - 500 Internal Server Error: API error
     - 502/503/504: Service unavailable
  
  5. **JsonException**
     - Invalid JSON response format
     - Deserialization failures
     - Missing required properties
end note

== Algorithm Behavior Examples ==

note over Caller, JSON
  **Example 1: Standard Case**
  - maxResults=100, pageSize=10, totalPages=15
  - Fetches pages 1-10 (100 workouts)
  - Stops when last20Workouts.Count == 100
  
  **Example 2: Partial Last Page**
  - maxResults=25, pageSize=10, totalPages=20
  - Page 1: adds 10 workouts (total: 10)
  - Page 2: adds 10 workouts (total: 20)
  - Page 3: adds 5 workouts (total: 25, remainingSlots=5)
  - Stops when maxResults reached
  
  **Example 3: Fewer Workouts Than Limit**
  - maxResults=100, pageSize=10, totalPages=3
  - Fetches all 3 pages (~30 workouts)
  - Stops when currentPage > totalPages
  - Returns fewer than maxResults
  
  **Example 4: Empty Response**
  - API returns null or empty workouts array
  - Loop breaks immediately
  - Returns empty or partial collection
end note

@enduml

